---
description: Keep Cursor edits isolated to its assigned Git worktree
alwaysApply: true
---

- Use the Cursor worktree assigned to this session in the root README. Keep
  edits, commits, and pushes on this worktree's branch. Do not edit another
  session's worktree, and do not edit `main` directly.
- Cursor desktop and CLI sessions are independent. Do not point two active
  Cursor writing sessions at the same worktree.
- After completing a requested task, review and commit/push only that task's
  finished changes. Leave unrelated or in-progress changes alone.
